Audio attribution
=================

Every voice clip in this game is a real person reading the same elicitation
paragraph, recorded for the Speech Accent Archive at George Mason University
(https://accent.gmu.edu/).

The original recordings and these shortened, loudness-normalized excerpts
(15 seconds each) are shared under the Creative Commons
Attribution-NonCommercial-ShareAlike 4.0 International license
(CC BY-NC-SA 4.0): https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-nc-sa/4.0/

Changes made: excerpts trimmed to 15 seconds, converted to mono, and
loudness-normalized. Speaker metadata (birthplace, first language, age and
sex) comes from each speaker's archive page.

This game is a non-commercial project. Do not use these clips commercially;
contact the archive or record your own voices for commercial use.
